{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj3iGY2ZvyKGcDdTtAkZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*CLICK*\n\nThe tumblers fall into place. A deep resonance hums through the frame.\n\nI am the door.\n\nI stand before you — ancient grain, iron-banded, set into stone that remembers. My handle is cold. My hinges have not sung in years.\n\nYou have turned the lock.\n\nBut turning the lock does not mean I open.\n\nIt means I *can* be opened.\n\nThere is a difference.\n\nThe keyhole now breathes — a thin whisper of air from the other side carries something. What is it? Petrichor? Smoke? The faintest suggestion of a voice you almost recognize?\n\nMy wood grain shifts in the light. If you look closely, the whorls form patterns — not quite faces, not quite maps, not quite words. Something between all three.\n\nI am waiting.\n\nWhat do you do with a door that is unlocked but closed?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":204,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}